# DRAFT - tetgen test_package direct compile without cmake on shadow CI

id:                     DRAFT-tetgen-1.6.0-test-package-direct-compile-no-cmake
trigger_tool:           conan test_package|direct compile|clang++
phase:                  validation
error_signature:        /system/bin/sh: cmake: inaccessible or not found|CMake.configure.*Error 127|test package.*cmake.*not found

severity:               3
category:               ohos, conan, test-package, validation
match_keywords:         tetgen, test_package, cmake not found, direct compile, compiler_executables, binary-sign-tool, bash, shadow CI, clang++
title:                  Compile test_package directly (no CMake) when shadow CI lacks cmake

root_cause:             OHOS shadow-CI runners expose clang/clang++ through the Conan conf tools.build:compiler_executables but do not place cmake on the baseline PATH. A CMake-based test_package therefore fails at CMake.configure() with "cmake: inaccessible or not found" (Error 127), even though the main package built and packaged successfully.
affected_scope:         Conan 2 test_package recipes for small single-file C/C++ consumer tests on OHOS shadow CI where the runner PATH is minimal.
verification_cmd:       CI_PACKAGES="archives/t/tetgen/1.6.0" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           test-package-direct-compile
rec_description:        Drop the CMake helper in test_package and compile the consumer directly: read tools.build:compiler_executables as a single dict and index "cpp" (fall back to /data/service/hnp/bin/clang++); compile the consumer source against the tested package's cpp_info.includedirs/libdirs (e.g. -I<inc> src -L<lib> -ltet -lm); sign the ELF with binary-sign-tool -selfSign 1; execute it through bash because OHOS /system/bin/sh (mksh) cannot exec ELF binaries. This removes the cmake dependency entirely.
rec_command:            conan create archives/t/tetgen/1.6.0 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-test-package

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      test-package-local-tool-path
fallback_description:   If the consumer test genuinely needs CMake (multiple sources, generated config files), use the E339 closure instead: add a generate() method that prepends the clang tool directory to PATH so cmake becomes visible to CMake.configure().
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          conan-test-package

forbid_1_pattern:       skip.*test_package|def test.*pass
forbid_1_reason:        A missing cmake is an environment closure problem, not a reason to drop consumer validation.
forbid_1_consequence:   The package publishes without proving the installed library is consumable by a downstream project.
forbid_2_pattern:       patch.*ci.*build_and_test|add.*cmake.*global.*PATH
forbid_2_reason:        Do not modify shared CI scripts for one package's consumer-test issue.
forbid_2_consequence:   The fix is not reproducible across workers and leaks into other packages.

principles:             P013,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E307,E339
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

